course: dictionary
lesson: 1037
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words wear different coats. The same word can name a place, a drink, and a colour. Bordeaux is one of these words. The context, the words around it, tells you which meaning is right. «Bordeaux is a port on a river in south-west France.» Here it is a place, a city you could visit on a map.
explain: «Lisbon, Oporto, and Bordeaux» is a list of places, so Bordeaux is a city again. A grown-up at dinner who says, «Pass the Bordeaux», is talking about a wine. If someone says, «Her coat was bordeaux», they mean a deep red colour, like the wine.
explain: Ask yourself: is this a thing, a drink or a colour? Then try each meaning in the sentence. The sentence will tell you which one fits best. Check it, just as you would with any new word.
fact: Bordeaux is a big city in south-west France, on the river Garonne.
fact: Bordeaux is also a red or white wine made in the area around Bordeaux. In the UK it is often called «claret».
fact: Bordeaux can also mean a deep red colour, like that wine.
fact: In French it is said bor-DOH. The «x» and «eau» are not said as they would be in English.
fact: A word with more than one meaning is called a word with several senses. Context tells you which sense is meant.
exercise: «Bordeaux is a port on a river in south-west France.» What is Bordeaux here? | *A city in France | A kind of cheese | A sea monster | A colour of paint
exercise: Mum says, «Pour me a glass of Bordeaux, please.» What is Bordeaux here? | A French verb | A river in Spain | *A red or white wine | A type of bread
exercise: Ella says, «Her front door is bordeaux.» What colour is the door? | Pale blue | *Deep red | Bright green | Bright yellow
test: In the sentence «Bordeaux is in France», which country is Bordeaux in? | Spain | *France | Portugal | Italy
test: Which is the right way to say Bordeaux in French? | *bor-DOH | BOR-dair | bor-DOX | bord-ee-oh
exam: In the list «Lisbon, Oporto, and Bordeaux», what kind of word is Bordeaux? | A sea creature | *A place name | Only a wine | A colour
